content.text:
Massive progress. The QA ran deep (mode=ending, step 12 shrine) but with issues:

1. `ERR phase warden/deepking/marshal: hurtMob null` — fightBoss called hurtMob on boss that already died (autoDlg closed scene) — but later phases still progressed because after err step++, skipping the assertions phases (warden/button assertions skipped → went directly to the NEXT phase, hence 'PASS sovereign spared' printed inside sovereign's err skip? no—sovereign spared printed, then deepking phase ERR...). The deepking phase crashed once then step++ moved on, so chapter asserts skipped but the game flow continued (onBossDead chains ran from autoDlg in later phases). Eventually reached shrine & ending!

Root cause in fightBoss: after boss dead (G.boss null), hurtMob(G.boss) called since ST flag set & `if (G.boss)`... wait fightBoss: `if (G.boss) {...hurtMob}` — G.boss should be null after death. Where's null? q: fightBoss('warden'): tick N: spawned (ST flag) — even if spawnBoss FAILED (chapter 1 gating? no — spawnMob boss = BOSSES[key] exists). Hmm hurtMob(m) with m null. That means `G.boss` non-null during check but null at call? No — single-threaded. OR the boss object a DIFFERENT check: `if (!ST['sp_'+key])` spawn — return. Then next tick: `if (G.boss) { G.p.hp=...; hurtMob(G.boss); }`. If G.boss null → no hurt. So hurtMob(null) implies G.boss truthy at check → G.boss set but hurtMob receives null?? No.

Look at stack: fightBoss line 33:54 → `hurtMob(G.boss)` in the `if (G.boss)` branch? Let me look at fightBoss code current:

```js
function fightBoss(key) {
  if (!ST['sp_' + key]) { ST['sp_' + key] = 1; spawnBoss(key, G.p.x + 60, G.p.y); return; }
  if (G.boss) { G.p.hp = G.p.maxhp; hurtMob(G.boss); hurtMob(G.boss); }
}
```

hurtMob → killMob if hp<=0 → boss kill → G.boss = null via killMob; the SECOND hurtMob(G.boss) call is the culprit! `hurtMob(G.boss); hurtMob(G.boss);` — first kills, G.boss=null → second crash. My bug. Fix: const b = G.boss; hurtMob(b); if (G.boss === b && !b.dead) hurtMob(b); Actually hurtMob(m) — m already captured: null only if I re-read G.boss. `hurtMob(G.boss); hurtMob(G.boss);` re-reads — yes that's it. Fix by capturing.

2. FAIL q_tea/q_lantern/q_remedy/q_ghost: the sidequest chain dialogs were interrupted: probably autoDlg didn't get to close before assertions? The assertion runs on first tick AFTER sq5 (q_toll) started... my sidequests phase: after sq5 runs Dlg.run('mara'), next tick autoDlg... after dialog closes, the phase continues to the asserts — q_toll done by then. But q_tea etc happened EARLIER — completed? 'verse: the asserts show q_toll PASS but others FAIL — meaning completion dialogs never processed: e.g. 'rowan' turn-in: `a.push(L(...), { do: () => { takeItem; advanceQuest; questReward }, go: '_close' })` — autoDlg processes lines → do-branch → with my new code: q0 capture — do() doesn't replace q → s.go '_close' → close. GOOD. So q_tea should complete...

UNLESS rowan's dialogue earlier (in NPC phase) marked q_tea offer choice idx0 'I'll gather them' → adds q_tea; then sidequests adds q_tea (no-op), giveItem moonpetal 3, Dlg.run('rowan') → should hit the invCount>=3 branch... invCount('moonpetal')≥3 → completion branch ✓.

Hmm so why FAIL? Let me think: the q_ghost chain: 'spirit' — q_ghost added in sidequests sq4; dialogue `if (!G.quests['q_ghost'])` — set → else return [L('Pale Spirit','One word...')] — my Dlg.run('spirit') run shows 'One word' line. Then q_ghost stays active. But sq4 doesn't reach the chain (_spirit2/3) because I SKIPPED the 'Finish your sentence' choice: after addQuest, dialogue goes to hunting line not the chain. So q_ghost never completes → FAIL (expected, my driver flaw).

But q_tea/q_lantern/q_remedy FAIL... Did the sidequests SQ steps actually run? The PASS sequence shows 'q_toll done' passed — the LAST step ran. So steps 1-4 ran too... The asserts run on the tick after sq5's dialog closes. Others should be done by then...

Unless the autoDlg didn't process the earlier dialogs fully before subsequent Dlg.run replaced them! Sequence issue: sq1 runs Dlg.run('rowan') and sets ST.sq1=1 in the SAME tick; next tick autoDlg processes rowan dialog... but 'if (autoDlg()) return;' at phase top — dialog advances. When close → next tick mode play → sq2 runs 'nima'... OK sequential. So each completion dialog closed. Hmm...

Wait — the L rows in npc phase: 'nima' first visit offers q_lantern choice AND — CRITICAL: at the property: sidequests q_lantern assertion requires `G.p.ownC.includes('lantern')` — reward only when turning in with the child's lantern — giveItem('childs_lantern',1), run('nima') — which branch? `G.quests['q_lantern'].done` false → else if invCount>0 → turn-in ✓.

So logically they should pass... unless the QLOG indicates these dialogs crashed mid-way. AutoDlg pick issues... For 'rowan' turn-in, the do goes: takeItem('moonpetal',3)... takeItem uses G.p.bag... fine.

OH WAIT. I see it: sq1 ran in the SAME tick — no wait. Consider autoDlg TRUE path: `if (autoDlg()) return;` — autoDlg returns true only if it ACTED. When mode play → false → continue. The FIRST tick of sidequests: mode play (previous phase closed). sq1: Dlg.run('rowan') → dialog opens. Next tick: autoDlg — advances one step. Multi-line dialog: rowan turn-in = [L('Moonpetals! Fresh...'), {do turn-in, go:_close}] → 2 ticks. Then close — mode play. sq2 'nima' etc. Total ~10 ticks. All good... but time: only 11 rAF frames irrelevant.

Hmm, BUT the phase asserts FAILed — meaning at asserts time q_tea.done false. What if Dlg.run('rowan') in sq1 hit the OTHER branch: `else if (G.quests['q_tea'].done)` no; `else if (invCount >=3)` — invCount('moonpetal') — G.p.bag — giveItem('moonpetal',3) — put in bag ✓. So completion branch. advanceQuest('q_tea') → q.s++ → s=1: QDB steps 2 → 1<2 → not complete... advanceQuest increments stage & completeQuest only when s>=steps.length. Rowan branch calls advanceQuest ONCE → s=1 < 2 → NOT done! The turn-in dialog in rowan does advanceQuest once — quest has 2 steps → q incomplete. So the game itself requires advanceQuest twice for q_tea?? Look at DLG.rowan turn-in: `{ do: () => { takeItem('moonpetal', 3); advanceQuest('q_tea'); questReward('q_tea'); }, go: '_close' }` — advanceQuest once → not complete → questReward called for an incomplete quest (rewards fine) but quest tracker shows step2 forever? Quest q_tea has steps: gather (1), bring (2). The dialogue gives items AND turn-in simultaneously — completing only stage 1. So the quest stays open forever → the tracker stays showing 'Bring them to Rowan.' — REAL GAME BUG #: quest never completes.

Fix: in DLG.rowan turn-in: advanceQuest('q_tea') twice (gather→turn-in), i.e., call advanceQuest twice, or simply completeQuest('q_tea'). Cleanest: completeQuest + questReward.

Same for q_lantern (2 steps: find lantern, return it): DLG.nima turn-in: advanceQuest once → incomplete. Fix: completeQuest.
q_remedy (2 steps): same bug → completeQuest.
q_toll: mara dialogue: idx0 → advanceQuest('q_toll') → 2 steps → s1 after still not complete! But q_toll PASSED in QA because mara's dialogue was called TWICE (npcs phase + sidequests sq5) — second advance completes. Note its reward... In q_toll dialogue: idx0 'The bandit took my coin' — completeQuest via advanceQuest second call. OK. But the reward path idx1 'I drove him off myself' calls completeQuest + reward directly. fine.

So fixes:
- DLG.rowan: in the turn-in do: `advanceQuest('q_tea'); advanceQuest('q_tea');`? cleaner: completeQuest('q_tea', silent?) + questReward. Use completeQuest (it toasts completion) + questReward.
- DLG.nima turn-in do: completeQuest('q_lantern'); questReward('q_lantern');
- DLG.hesan turn-in do: completeQuest('q_remedy'); questReward('q_remedy');
- q_well similar? well1 branch: completeQuest('q_well') directly ✓ (well dialog did `{ do: () => { completeQuest('q_well'); questReward('q_well'); }, go: '_close' }`) ✓.
- q_ghost chain: completeQuest ✓ present. So the prior FAIL is due driver (skip chain). Driver: start spirit dialog fresh (quest NOT added): Dlg.run('spirit') offers choice idx0 → chain. In sq4 I pre-addQuest then run → dead-end line. Fix driver: DON'T pre-add for spirit; autoDlg idx0 adds quest then chain runs automatically. (choice cond! there's no cond; fine.)

3. 'well grants ring charm' FAIL: second wellDialog... logic: after first: F('well1') set & q_well.done → second call: `if (!G.quests['q_well']) ... if done → Dlg.run('well'); return;` — the well dialog ENDS the flow after quest done — well2 unreachable in wellDialog! Look at wellDialog:

```js
if (!G.quests['q_well']) { Dlg.run('well'); return; }
if (G.quests['q_well'].done) { Dlg.run('well'); return; }
if (!F('well1')) { ... well1 chain with completeQuest... }
else if (!F('well2')) {... }
```
After first chain, q_well.done=true → second call short-circuits to flavor → ring branch unreachable. REAL BUG: the well's second wish (ring) inaccessible once quest completed. Fix: move the 'done → run(well) flavor' to AFTER both tosses: if not done → toss branches; flavor only when both well1 & well2 done. Rewrite:

```js
function wellDialog() {
  const toss = ...;
  if (!G.quests['q_well']) { Dlg.run('well'); return; }
  if (!F('well1')) { ... } else if (!F('well2')) { ... } else Dlg.run('well');
}
```
i.e., remove the `if (done) { run('well'); return; }` line. But the first branch requires coins 10 (toss handles insufficient coins with toast; throw if no coins → toast). Coins in QA plenty. OK.

Also in the first branch's chain: after tossing (toss happens at do step {do toss}), + L('Pip'), + {do complete...}, with my next() fix: do → s.go? none → next... LAST version: `{ do: () => { completeQuest('q_well'); questReward('q_well'); }, go: '_close' }` → after my fix, do → go '_close' → close. good.

4. 'PASS shrine awake' REPEATED FOREVER + step stuck at shrine — after shrine asserts + goto + interact → finale dialog chain; but autoDlg never advances because... `if (autoDlg()) return;` then ST.shr already 1 → asserts pass each tick → goto + interact EVERY TICK (re-entering finale? Since got finale_at after first interact — subsequent interact hits else toast 'The Heart pulses patiently.' — fine, and Game.goto repeatedly... but the finale dialog... the autoDlg should advance: finale_enter L1 L2 L3 do → L?? {go:'finale'} → DLG.finale() → choices → PICKHINT null → idx0 →'«Give the Ember to the Marshal»' when pact_offer → doEnding('ash')?? Wait arc appears counter shows mode=ending ch=2/2 — so autoDlg DID advance into... 'ash'?? q picked idx0... mode ending... So the driver picked the ASH ending (marh?) Because PICKHINT null in shrine (idx0 pact). Then mode 'ending' → shrine phase loops (asserts each tick & goto & interact — mode not play so interact early-returns... but phase never 'NEXT's because it expects endingShared stage). Because the ending happened in the SHrine phase (premature pick), endingShared never sees what it expects. Then stuck.

Driver design flaw: shrine phase should handle the ending: after interact, if mode 'dialog' autoDlg with hint /kiln/. Partition: shrine asserts then set ST.hx=1 and return; subsequent helper... simpler: since PICKHINT for kiln needed during ANY phase, set PICKHINT globally once shrine done (i.e., from shrine phase set PICKHINT=/kiln/). Then endingShared phase can be: if mode 'dialog' → autoDlg (already handled?)... Actually autoDlg runs INSIDE shrine phase ticks as top — wait order: top of shrine: `if (autoDlg()) return;` — with PICKHINT set AFTER ST.shr run... the interacting happens in same tick as Dlg.run('shrine')? No: shrine phase from tick A: ST.shr set; Dlg.run('shrine') → mode dialog. ticks: autoDlg advances shrine dialog → closes → next tick asserts → goto & interact → finale chain dialog (do F finale_at + go finale) → choices. From the SAME tick? The `Game.interact()` runs synchronously creating dialog; W(2) sets waits — with waits the next 2 ticks defer the BODY but autoDlg still processed? NO — the wait check happens BEFORE the body (interval wrapper). So the finale dialog won't advance during 'shrine' phase waits, and the THEN phase ends? The shrine phase ends only by error/never — because it has no 'NEXT'.

Restructure the shrine phase:

```js
