Why did interact not start the finale? Look: interact case 'heart': `if (G.chapter >= 5 && !got('finale_at'))` — G.chapter >= 5 ✓ (marshal done). deleted flag ✓. — so the chain Dlg.runArray... should open dialog. UNLESS findFocus failed: player position after continueGame — continueGame loaded save: the save snapshot was taken... WHEN? Save states: autosave/saveGame during earlier phases — the last saveGame happened at various points: afterBoss saveGame(true) — that stores map,=x,y,snapshot at MARSHAL death scene — location: keep near boss area? G.spawnPt updated by tryBoss... The QA didn't move player after that. saveGame stores G.p.x — at marshal fight: G.p.x=... the marshal boss spawn position (player.x+60...). coordinates from 'mobsmoke' phase spawn: player was at keep (20,20)*16=328,340 region. Boss at player+60. So the SAVE placed player at (388, 352-ish px) — NOT at the heart! Then in finaleShared: ST.heart → Game.goto('keep', 20*TILE+8, 2*TILE+10) — set pos at heart → interact via Game.interact()... which finds focus ✓ first finale ran fine.

Then endLoadBtn → continueGame → loadInto() REPLACED G.p again with SAVED coords (heart? did anything save after the goto? saveGame(true) happens in... G.pendingSave & camp saves; finale entering does not save. The last actual saveGame call: afterBoss (chapter5 + toast) — WAIT: afterBoss('marshal') → saveGame(true). Yes! That was during marshal end dialog: player pos = marshal fight position (328+60? — boss spawn x +60 from G.p.x at fight time...). Whatever — after continueGame the player is at the FIGHT position, NOT the heart.

finaleUnwritten tick1: `if (!ST.asked) { delete finale_at; Game.interact(); W(2); }` — player not at heart → findFocus null → no dialog → returns; subsequent ticks: ST.asked truthy → W(3) loop forever. That's the stall: forgot to re-position at heart.

